From: alesx2io <96351978+alesx2io@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:44:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dash: use the AOSP auto brightness timing

The stock light sensor debounce (1 s) and ambient light horizons (1.5 s /
1 s) are tuned for the HyperOS brightness algorithm. With the AOSP
controller auto brightness followed every short shadow on the
under-display sensor: looking at the front camera made the screen swing
between about 220 and 600 nits.

Use the AOSP defaults: 4 s / 8 s debounce (drop the overlay values) and
10 s / 2 s horizons (blob fixup of the display config).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 extract-files.py                                    |  5 +++++
 overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml | 10 +++-------
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/extract-files.py b/extract-files.py
index ce3e4f8..eaf7d0d 100755
--- a/extract-files.py
+++ b/extract-files.py
@@ -141,6 +141,11 @@ def blob_fixup_displayconfig(
         data = data.replace(ramp_anchor, ramps + ramp_anchor, 1)
     if threshold_anchor in data and 'ambientBrightnessChangeThresholds' not in data:
         data = data.replace(threshold_anchor, threshold_anchor + thresholds, 1)
+    # The stock 1.5 s / 1 s ambient light horizons are tuned for the HyperOS brightness
+    # algorithm. With the AOSP controller they make auto brightness follow every short
+    # shadow on the under-display sensor; use the AOSP defaults instead.
+    data = data.replace(ramp_anchor, '    <ambientLightHorizonLong>10000</ambientLightHorizonLong>\n', 1)
+    data = data.replace(threshold_anchor, '    <ambientLightHorizonShort>2000</ambientLightHorizonShort>\n', 1)
 
     with open(file_path, 'w') as f:
         f.write(data)
diff --git a/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml
index 542b4f7..c57e89d 100644
--- a/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/DashFrameworksOverlay/res/values/config.xml
@@ -62,13 +62,9 @@
          Must be in the range specified by minimum and maximum. -->
     <item name="config_screenBrightnessSettingDefaultFloat" format="float" type="dimen">0.07496032</item>
 
-    <!-- Stability requirements in milliseconds for accepting a new brightness level.  This is used
-         for debouncing the light sensor.  Different constants are used to debounce the light sensor
-         when adapting to brighter or darker environments.  This parameter controls how quickly
-         brightness changes occur in response to an observed change in light level that exceeds the
-         hysteresis threshold. -->
-    <integer name="config_autoBrightnessBrighteningLightDebounce">1000</integer>
-    <integer name="config_autoBrightnessDarkeningLightDebounce">1000</integer>
+    <!-- config_autoBrightness{Brightening,Darkening}LightDebounce: use the AOSP defaults
+         (4 s / 8 s). The stock 1 s values made auto brightness follow every short shadow on
+         the under-display light sensor, e.g. the user's head while using the front camera. -->
 
     <!-- The maximum range of gamma adjustment possible using the screen
          auto-brightness adjustment setting. -->
